        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a8e49023-1a39-53d0-afce-e0f5cd612c77",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kenneth Williams, Michael Sheen, Cheryl Campbell, Lou, Bob Hoskins, Christopher Lambert, Andie MacDowell, Ralph Richardson, Ian Holm, James Fox, Ian Charleson\n- Works: Kenneth Williams: Fantabulosa!, Pennies From Heaven, Testament of Youth, Malice Aforethought, A Doll's House, Greystoke: The Legend of Tarzan, Lord of the Apes\n- Organizations: BBC Four, BBC, BAFTA, Olivier Awards\n- Roles: Kenneth Williams, Lou, Tarzan, Jane\n\nFacts:\n- Cheryl Campbell was born on 22 May 1949 and is an English actor of stage, film, and television.\n- In 1978, Cheryl Campbell starred opposite Bob Hoskins in the BBC drama Pennies From Heaven.\n- In 1980, Cheryl Campbell won the BAFTA TV Award for Best Actress for Testament of Youth and Malice Aforethought.\n- In 1982, Cheryl Campbell won the Olivier Award for Best Actress in a Revival for A Doll's House.\n- Kenneth Williams: Fantabulosa! is a 2006 BBC Four television play starring Michael Sheen as the English comic actor Kenneth Williams and is based on Williams's own diaries.\n- In Kenneth Williams: Fantabulosa!, Cheryl Campbell plays Kenneth Williams's beloved mother, Lou.\n- In Greystoke: The Legend of Tarzan, Lord of the Apes, Christopher Lambert stars as Tarzan, although the name Tarzan is never used in the film's dialogue, and Andie MacDowell stars as Jane.\n- The cast of Greystoke: The Legend of Tarzan, Lord of the Apes also includes Ralph Richardson in his final film appearance, Ian Holm, James Fox, Cheryl Campbell, and Ian Charleson.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "de47030c-a6fb-5676-901c-404dd517019e",
        "text": "Page: Kenneth Williams: Fantabulosa!. Sentence: is a 2006 BBC Four television play starring Michael Sheen as the English comic actor Kenneth Williams, based on Williams' own diaries.\nPage: Kenneth Williams: Fantabulosa!. Sentence: Cheryl Campbell plays Williams's beloved mother, Lou.\nPage: Cheryl Campbell. Sentence: Cheryl Campbell (born 22 May 1949) is an English actor of stage, film and television.\nPage: Cheryl Campbell. Sentence: She starred opposite Bob Hoskins in the 1978 BBC drama \"Pennies From Heaven\", before going on to win the 1980 BAFTA TV Award for Best Actress for \"Testament of Youth\" and \"Malice Aforethought\", and the 1982 Olivier Award for Best Actress in a Revival for \"A Doll's House\".\nPage: Greystoke: The Legend of Tarzan, Lord of the Apes. Sentence: Christopher Lambert stars as Tarzan (though the name Tarzan is never used in the film's dialogue) and Andie MacDowell as Jane; the cast also includes Ralph Richardson (in his final film appearance), Ian Holm, James Fox, Cheryl Campbell, and Ian Charleson.",
